  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A working frontier, clearly observed",
    "overview": "Platonik gives the game a physical identity: sun-warmed ground, worn copper and teal machines, ore seams, spark crystals, and small courier rovers. The surrounding interface stays quiet enough to inspect their work. The game is an Experience surface with an Operate workshop; it uses the same accessible controls and reading voice as the rest of the site.\n\nThe shared site system remains intact. The homepage uses the Hraness editorial marketing treatment, documentation uses restrained reading columns, and archived laboratories retain their data-derived diagrams. Original raster art replaces abstract physical-world markers on the current frontier; it does not replace the laboratories' scientific encodings. The surface-specific composition is recorded in `.impeccable/surfaces/app-play.md`.",
